  186     /// The failed entry's exact name bytes when they are not the text's —
  187     /// set where the failure is made, so a name that collides with another
  188     /// in its lossy text still names its own file (review cr-jl3afix1-1).
  189     pub raw_relative_path: Option<Vec<u8>>,
  190     /// D-2026-11-24-1: the failure left this run's own incomplete copy at
  191     /// the destination — set where that is known, never read from
  192     /// `reason`, which is for people.
  193     pub left_in_place: bool,
  194     /// cr-ecm36-3: `relative_path` is the report's shortened rendering of a
  195     /// longer name — for people only; the exact name is in the failed-path
  196     /// set. Read back from a peer's report; never set where a failure is
