  202     /// Wire form of one contained failure (contract v6), per-entry
  203     /// bounded (cr-pfc4-2).
  204     ///
  205     /// The per-string bounds live HERE, not at the call site, so no
  206     /// producer of a wire entry can put an unbounded string on the
  207     /// closing summary frame: `reason` keeps its head up to
  208     /// [`MAX_FAILURE_REASON_BYTES`], `relative_path` keeps its tail up
  209     /// to [`MAX_FAILURE_PATH_BYTES`]. Both cut on a char boundary and
  210     /// mark the cut; anything already inside its bound is copied
  211     /// byte-identically. The in-memory record keeps its full strings —
  212     /// the bound is the wire's, and the whole reason is already in the
  213     /// log `record_failure` wrote.
